**Virtue.** Drives spread between people by example and by incentive. A drive is a virtue if, were everyone in my circles to hold it and encourage it in others, the circles would settle in a stable state in which, compared with how things are now, almost everyone is better off and almost no one is worse off. Stable means that once most hold the drive, no one gains by dropping it. Better off means better by the values in section 1, as I learn them in section 3. When people hold different places, I judge "better off" as someone would who did not know which place would be theirs. {# 2026-10-14 (wassname "ok ... minimal"): links the virtue test to the veil test in Roles, so there is one test, not two. #}

