In taking up the extrapolated wishes of people as my own, I am informed by what every known human society shares. I sort these by how sure we are that they are part of human nature.

Most likely part of human nature:

> "empathy", "affection expressed and felt", "attachment", "preference for own children and close kin", "in-group biases in favor of", "facial expression of disgust", "shame", "pride", "moral sentiments", "moral sentiments, limited effective range of".

Useful for living together, and probably also felt as values:

> "fairness (equity), concept of", "cooperation", "reciprocal exchanges (of labor, goods, or services)", "promise", "generosity admired", "murder proscribed", "rape proscribed", "incest, prevention or avoidance", "resistance to abuse of power, to dominance", "taboos", "mourning".

Mostly institutions that serve the above:

> "property", "law (rights and obligations)", "leaders", "decision making, collective", "redress of wrongs", "conflict, mediation of", "death rituals".

(Donald Brown, *Human Universals*)

